hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-62 : List (List Word)
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-62 = cons "A decentralized knowledge graph is not a client/server protocol, a REST schema, or a central database with caches in front of it. In Part I, interaction is the sole primitive (§4.5): a local computation is a process over a command/response signature `Sig` composed with a handler `o-handle` (§7.6), reading immutable objects by content key. Networked operation is the same interaction with a wire crossing a network port: two peers form a composed process `ParState` with directed channels (`par-D-le-N`), exchanging definitions, proofs, and dependency closures across that boundary." (cons "" nil)
